Docker Runtime Configuration

## What I did
- Ran container on a different host port:
  docker run -p 8085:9090 backend-demo
- Verified application using new port
- Ran container in detached mode:
  docker run -d -p 9090:9090 backend-demo
- Listed running containers using:
  docker ps
- Stopped container using:
  docker stop <container_id>

## Key Learnings
- Port mapping allows multiple environments to run the same container
- Detached mode enables background execution
- Container lifecycle can be managed using docker commands

## Architect Insight
Understanding container runtime behavior helps in managing applications across development, testing, and production environments.
